  "webEntry": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <!-- maximum-scale/user-scalable are NOT cosmetic here: without them, tapping\n         the pop composer's message field permanently breaks the map's layout.\n         iOS WebKit auto-zooms the page whenever a text field with a computed\n         font-size UNDER 16px takes focus, and `.composeMessage` is a 10px\n         textarea. WebKit does not undo that zoom on blur, so the whole UI stays\n         scaled up with its right-hand side \u2014 \"Post here\", the radius total \u2014\n         clipped off the screen until the app is relaunched. Pinning the scale is\n         the only lever that covers every such field at once, and it costs\n         nothing the app wants: Mapbox drives pinch-zoom from its own touch\n         handlers, not from page scale, so the map still zooms normally.\n         WKWebView honours this because `ignoresViewportScaleLimits` is left at\n         its default of false \u2014 if that is ever set true, this bug comes back. -->\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\" />\n    <!-- The base background of a document \u2014 what WebKit paints BEFORE any author\n         CSS applies \u2014 is white unless the document declares a dark colour scheme.\n         This meta is honoured while the head is still parsing, earlier than the\n         inline style below and far earlier than the bundle's stylesheet, so it is\n         the only lever that covers the very first paint. It matters most for this\n         page as an IFRAME (the map embed): a subframe's base background paints\n         ABOVE the iframe element's own background, so the parent cannot colour it. -->\n    <meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"dark\" />\n    <title>Poplur \u2014 Post-login</title>\n    <!-- Mapbox's stylesheet is imported in main.tsx and bundled, NOT fetched\n         from api.mapbox.com. A cross-origin <link> here is render-blocking on\n         every launch: the shell serves from local assets, so this was a DNS +\n         TLS + fetch round trip before first paint, and on a slow or offline\n         phone it blocked until the request gave up. It is 40KB. -->\n\n    <style>\n      *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n      html { color-scheme: dark; }\n      html, body, #root { width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #050407; }\n    </style>\n    <script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"./index-WVaJoPa0.js\"></script>\n    <link rel=\"modulepreload\" crossorigin href=\"./react-DZRUXSPQ.js\">\n    <link rel=\"modulepreload\" crossorigin href=\"./three-CF7bMts2.js\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"./index-DZGLsgVn.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
